{
  "$comment": "Read by hooks/dist/rule-router.mjs. Each entry loads its rule files the FIRST time a matching tool call happens in a session. mode 'deny-first' refuses that first call with the rule text as the reason (for rules that must change the decision); \"subagent\": \"block\" marks a spend or confirm-first gate that also blocks every fresh subagent once (without it, a subagent gets the rule as an inject after the session had the block); 'inject' adds the text as context and lets the call run. Matchers: command = regexes tested against each command segment with quoted strings removed and leading env/&/cmd /c prefixes dropped; segment = regexes tested against each executed segment with quotes KEPT (for quoted script paths; anchor them with ^ so an echo of the text never claims the rule); agent = subagent_type; skill = Skill name; tools = tool_name (MCP tools). Keep the always-loaded index rules-src/on-demand-rules.md in step with this file.",
